{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:1.1", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "1.1"}, "paraphrase": "As the vowel 'a' pervades all letters, the Lord, without equal, pervades everything as knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "original": {"text": "அகர உயிர்போல் அறிவாகி எங்கும் நிகரில் இறைநிற்கும் நிறைந்து", "script": "Tamil", "edition": "from memory; to be checked"}, "concepts": ["cpt:siddhanta-advaita"], "cross_refs": ["tea:tirukkural:1"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.10", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.10"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on those who have attained (aṇaintōr taṉmai): the freed live without 'I' and 'mine', their acts are Śiva's acts, and they neither seek nor reject.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ethics"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.3", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.3"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on the dark mala (iruḷ-mala-nilai): āṇava is one, beginningless and hides the soul's knowledge as darkness hides objects — but, unlike darkness, it hides itself as well; it is removed not by the soul's effort but by grace.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:anava-mala"], "obstacles": ["obs:anava-mala"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.4", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.4"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on grace (aruḷatu-nilai): grace is always present with the soul, as the sun's light is to the eye, yet the soul does not see it while covered by mala; grace is Śiva's own power.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:arul"], "concepts": ["cpt:grace-anugraha"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference; the sun image is recalled at moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.5", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.5"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on grace embodied (aruḷ-uru-nilai): as a deer is caught with a decoy deer, Śiva takes human form as the guru to catch souls who know only human forms.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru-as-siva"], "notes": "Chapter-level; the decoy image is recalled at moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:tiruvarutpayan:ch.9", "source": "src:tiruvarutpayan", "location": {"ref": "ch.9"}, "paraphrase": "The chapter on the five letters (aintheḻuttu-aruḷ-nilai): the right order of the five letters places grace between Śiva and the soul, and meditating them so leads the soul to Śiva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:pancaksara"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U18-saiva-siddhanta"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
